@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;design;motion] library-one-foot-bar
Library destinations MUST register their bar through FootPill or FootFree. One
FootBarLayer in the shell draws the active registration over the pages. A page change
MUST keep that layer in place; the contents change through Pully's blur fade and the
pill's width eases to its new size. Disposed registrations MUST stop owning the bar.
Source: pulls.review kit-one-foot-bar, DESIGN rule 196, FootBar.kt at
ee5cf358333cb1170f1923c7118e12af3f265b74; requested by Tavi on 22 October 2026.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;motion;architecture] library-search-morphs-the-navigation
All, Spaces and Search MUST show the same bar: one FootPill with one round
button, FootCircle, beside it. The tabs and the search field MUST be contents of that
pill, never a capsule or pill of their own, and Search and Close MUST be glyphs of that
circle. Opening or closing search MUST keep the one pill and the one circle on the same
line and at the same height: the pill widens from its two icons to the full width,
carrying the circle to the end, and narrows back when search closes, while the tabs
blur out as the field blurs in and the magnifier with a sparkle turns into the close
cross, through Pully's blur fade. A page that adds its own bar MUST do so through the
same pill and circle.
Source: Tavi, 28 October 2026 ("the bottom bar of the search and spaces isn't the same
one as it is on the everything section. if you look at pully, you will see that the
best is to use exactly the same one and morph it depending on the page");
pulls.review kit-one-foot-bar. The pill widening replaced "in place and at the same
size" when Tavi picked version 03 of the Everything bar on 1 November 2026 ("Yeah!
Let's use 03").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] library-bars-rest-alike
Every library foot bar MUST use floatingBar for its position: 12dp in from the sides,
16dp above the system navigation bar, and raised by the keyboard. Screens MUST NOT
add their own bottom offset to the bar. The bar floats over the content without a
solid strip behind it and carries Pully's two-layer downward canvas shadow. The pill
and the circle beside it are 56dp tall on every page, search included, with an 8dp
highlight inset around the tabs (made one height for search on 28 October 2026, when
Tavi asked for one bar on every page).
Source: pulls.review kit-bottom-bars-rest-alike, DESIGN rules 192 and 45, Kit.kt at
ee5cf358333cb1170f1923c7118e12af3f265b74; geometry from Tavi's Google Photos
comparison in the recorded review of 22 October 2026 ("less tall", "start a bit
further to the left", "a bit wider").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;motion] library-bar-leaves-for-full-screen
A page that goes full screen, as a gallery does at one column, MUST register it with
the shell's ShellImmersion. As far as the page has gone full screen, the bar slides down
past the bottom of the screen and fades, out of reach of taps, and the shell's paper turns
black with light status and navigation bar icons. A page that never goes full screen
leaves the bar where library-bars-rest-alike puts it.
Source: Tavi, 30 October 2026, the gallery's full-screen mode ("we full screen one thing").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] library-foot-bar-owns-its-taps
A tap anywhere inside the search pill, including its edge and padding, MUST focus
its field or expand its compact form. A tap on the navigation capsule's padding
MUST NOT open a card underneath it. Search and navigation controls MUST have touch
targets of at least 44dp.
Source: pulls.review kit-foot-bar-owns-its-taps, DESIGN rule 198, FootBar.kt at
ee5cf358333cb1170f1923c7118e12af3f265b74.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design;motion] library-navigation-is-the-gallery-capsule
The library navigation pill MUST offer All and Spaces as two icon tabs, with
Search as a separate circular control showing a magnifier with a sparkle, drawn after
Google Photos' AI search (Ask) glyph: the ring open at its top right with a four-point
sparkle in the gap, in round-capped strokes, about 22dp in the 56dp circle. It MUST NOT
add a Create tab. The pill is only as wide as its two tabs and sits centred with the
circle beside it, leaving the corners of the screen to the cards. The chosen tab shows
its filled icon on the selected highlight, the other its outline icon in a dark grey.
Changing the tab MUST show the chosen place's name beside its icon for about a second
and a half and then fold it away, the pill growing and shrinking with it; arriving on
a page or closing search MUST NOT show a name. The names MUST stay readable by
accessibility services while folded. Each tab keeps the pill's full height to tap.
When system animations are disabled the highlight and the name MUST change at once.
Changing the selected tab MUST preserve the one bar registration rather than creating
a second visible bar.
Source: Tavi's pick of version 03, "Two icons, names on change", from the 15 Everything
bars, 1 November 2026 ("Yeah! Let's use 03"), which replaced the Google Photos capsule
with both labels of 22 and 23 October 2026; Tavi's no-Create decision, 22 October 2026.
The glyph was redrawn after Google Photos' when Tavi said on 6 November 2026 that "the
search icon is not quite like the Google Photos one" and that it keeps its sparkle ("It's
the new AI search"); its proportions and size were measured by Claude from a Google Photos
screenshot and are Claude's choice.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;motion] library-steps-back-behind-the-reader
While a card's reader is open, ShellFrame MUST draw the page and its bar as one card
that steps back as far as the reader's sheet is up (`card-reader-rises-as-a-sheet`),
on black, and MUST come forward with the sheet as it sinks or is pulled down. Anything
drawn over the page as an overlay stays where it is.
Source: Tavi's pick of 13 and 14 on the card opening page, 30 October 2026 ("Let's do
13 and 14 together"), transitions.dev's Banner stacking.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] library-pages-swipe-side-by-side
All, Spaces and Ask MUST sit side by side in the bar's order, Ask (the search the
circle opens) last, through SidePages, ported from Pully's: a sideways drag anywhere a page
does not use itself moves both pages exactly with the finger, nothing fading or blurring,
and letting go settles on the nearer page, or on the next one the way a throw went once the
finger has moved it part of the way, on Pully's critically damped page spring. A tab or the
circle glides the row to its page. The bar MUST change with the page as the finger lets go,
through library-navigation-is-the-gallery-capsule and library-search-morphs-the-navigation.
Arriving on Ask, by the circle or by a swipe, MUST put the cursor in its field (Tavi,
5 November 2026: "When I swipe over to the search screen, the search input should be
automatically focused"); only Same Vibe's similar cards open it with the keyboard down. Closing
Ask goes back to the page it was opened from. Two fingers are a pinch and MUST NOT turn a
page; a page in full screen (library-bar-leaves-for-full-screen) MUST NOT swipe, and a
page's full screen MUST only hide the bar while that page is on screen. Each page keeps its
scroll and column count while away, and the page beside the one on screen is built ahead so
a swipe never holds at its start.
Source: Tavi, 5 November 2026 ("I want to be able to swipe between the everything, spaces,
and ask pages. Should feel seamless to go from one to another. Just as it does in Pully");
pulls.review kit-side-pages-slide-whole, kit-side-pages-keep-state and
kit-drags-carry-on-or-settle.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;motion] scroll-views-blur-their-edges
Every scrolling view in the app MUST blur and fade its content into the page at the
top once it has scrolled away from its start, and at the bottom while more lies below:
the galleries (All, Ask's results, the Spaces list and an opened space) through
gallery-top-edge-blurs-the-scrolling-content and the mosaic's foot fade, and every
other scrolling column (Ask before anything is typed, the search dock's answer, the
sheets, the reader and its name card) through `scrollEdgeFade`. At rest at an edge,
that edge stays sharp. The reader's foot keeps its own fade under its buttons instead.
Source: Tavi, 5 November 2026 ("If there's a scroll view, we have blur at the top and
at the bottom when it's scrolled ... We are, in fact, also not doing it in the spaces").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] gallery-tab-is-called-all
The tab of the whole library, mymind's Everything, MUST be named "All" wherever the app
shows or speaks it, such as the bar's tab and the reader's Back to All; contracts call
that page All too. The code keeps the enum `Tab.Everything`.
Source: Tavi, 5 November 2026 ("Rename it to 'All'"), picked over Mind, Home and All
cards when asked what to call Everything.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design;architecture] window-shapes-follow-pully
The app MUST read its window as one of three shapes (WindowShape): narrower than 600dp is a
phone and MUST look exactly as before; 600dp or wider but under 600dp tall is a phone held
sideways; at least 600dp both ways is unfolded (a foldable opened, a tablet). Sideways, one
page shows at a time and the library's pages sit in a column no wider than ReadableWidth,
centred, with the page colour either side, and the foot bar is no wider than that column.
Unfolded, ShellFrame MUST show the gallery with its foot bar on the left, a little under half
the width and between 340 and 420dp (listPaneWidth), a hairline, and the opened card beside
it as a page of its own rather than a sheet over a stepped-back gallery; with nothing open
the right pane shows only one muted line saying a card you open shows there. Opening another
card from the gallery replaces the one beside it. Every shape MUST keep pages clear of a
camera cutout or navigation bar at the side, and turning the phone or opening the foldable
MUST keep the open card, page and scroll (the activity handles the change itself rather than
being recreated).
Source: Tavi, 5 November 2026 ("Let's also follow Pully in how it adapted its layouts for
foldable phones and rotated states a while ago (look into it), and do that for this as
well"); pulls.review unfolded-window-reads-one-stack-as-two-panes and
wide-window-pages-keep-a-readable-column, DESIGN rules 206, 207 and 209 (PR #137).
